course: dictionary
lesson: 14633
title: Powdery
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Powdery is an adjective. It describes something that is like powder: fine, dry and soft, as if it could be blown away in a puff of air. Look for the clues in the sentence. «The chalk left a powdery mark on my fingers.» Chalk is dry and fine, and it rubs off easily, so powdery describes that kind of soft, dusty texture.
explain: Powdery can also mean covered with powder. «The table was powdery with flour after the baking.» The flour lies all over the table, so the table is covered with a fine dusting. Ask yourself: what is the thing like, and is it covered in something? Then try the meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Powdery is different from wet or sticky. Snow that is wet and heavy packs into balls. Snow that is powdery is dry and light, so it is soft and fine. Skiers love it because it feels like soft dust under their skis.
fact: Powdery means like powder: fine, dry and soft.
fact: Powdery can also mean covered with powder.
fact: «Powdery» is an adjective, and its forms are powdery, more powdery and most powdery.
fact: Flour and chalk are powdery solids, so they are good examples of the word.
fact: «Powdery snow» is dry, light snow that is soft and fine, and skiers love it.
exercise: «The chalk left a powdery mark on my fingers.» What does powdery mean here? | *Like powder, fine and dry | Very loud | Hard as a rock | Wet and sticky
exercise: Skiers love powdery snow. Which snow is powdery? | Snow that has melted into slush | *Fine, dry and soft snow | Snow that is hard and icy | Snow that is brown with mud
exercise: «The table was powdery with flour after the baking.» What does powdery mean in this sentence? | *Covered with powder | Painted bright red | Wet with rain | Polished and shiny
test: «The sand was powdery and warm under our bare feet.» What does powdery mean? | Cold and wet | *Like powder: fine, dry and soft | Full of sharp stones | Hard and rough
test: Which of these is a powdery solid? | Water | A wooden block | A metal spoon | *Chalk
exam: «The baker's hands were white and powdery after kneading the dough.» What does powdery mean? | *Like powder, fine and dry | Warm from the oven | Sticky with honey | Heavy and wet
